 ## The harvest
 
-Artifacts return to the corpus through harvesters: pure functions
-from a landed artifact to a corpus mutation (adopt a topic, grow
-a fragment, file a gloss), invoked from one dispatch keyed on
-completions rather than five state machines polling `landed()`.
-Every harvester is re-derivable: cache plus corpus reproduces the
-same adoptions in the same order on any machine, any session --
-determinism is what makes the cache a proof rather than a risk.
+Artifact availability and adoption admission are separate nodes.
+A landed artifact marks its artifact id done and pokes.  Each
+adoptable artifact has a local agenda action
+`H("adopt", artifact id, generation witness)` whose dependencies
+are the artifact id and every witness governing that adoption.
+The local lane takes ready actions and invokes one compile-time
+harvester table; cache hits complete artifacts, never bypass their
+adoption actions. Every harvester converts exact artifact bytes into
+immutable facts keyed by artifact id.  Completion is only a wakeup:
+the generated projection folds those facts by a canonical, corpus-derived 
+order, never callback order.  Sequential display identities are assigned
+after that ordering; incremental folds are allowed only when their
+merge is associative, commutative and idempotent.
 
